  "title": "Unified title",
  "summary": "FedS2R presents a one-shot federated domain generalization framework for synthetic-to-real semantic segmentation in autonomous driving, combining inconsistency-driven data augmentation and multi-client knowledge distillation to achieve state-of-the-art results.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "FedS2R integrates an inconsistency-driven data augmentation strategy to generate synthetic images for unstable classes, and a multi-client knowledge distillation scheme with feature fusion to distill a global model.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Experiments on five real-world datasets show that the global model significantly outperforms individual client models, with only a 2 mIoU gap to the fully shared model.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "FedS2R addresses the need for synthetic-to-real semantic segmentation in autonomous driving by leveraging federated learning techniques.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
